{
  "abstract": "For abstract linear control systems on Banach spaces with L-infinity inputs, the operator norm of the input map tends to zero at time zero, and every input response is continuous on the nonnegative time axis. The hypotheses are strong continuity of the semigroup, bounded linear input maps, and the concatenation identity; no integral representation is assumed. The proof uses a diagonal consequence of Phillips' lemma, proved in the repository, and a semigroup doubling argument. This gives a positive answer to Weiss' 1989 Problem 2.4.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Frédéric Marbach"
    }
  ],
